## Notes for Future Sessions

1. **Always test all API versions** — older versions (pre-2020) often have weaker validation
2. **Auth bypass is the key** — most high-impact vectors are gated behind 401; focus on bypass first
3. **SAML/JWT bearer grants** — highest deserialization risk, test thoroughly
4. **CSP analysis** — check both enforce and report-only modes; `unsafe-inline`/`unsafe-eval` enable XSS
5. **Cookie flags** — missing HttpOnly + SameSite on session cookies = session theft via XSS
6. **Link headers** — always check for framework path leakage
7. **Internal ports** — redirects to non-standard ports (8443) indicate internal infrastructure
8. **Parameter pollution** — test duplicate params on OAuth endpoints specifically
9. **Content-Type confusion** — test XML/JSON/multipart on all POST endpoints
10. **Document taint flows** — source → sink traces enable exploit chain construction